tps://godotengine.org/\nOpenGL API 3.3.0 NVIDIA 591.74 - Compatibility - Using Device: NVIDIA - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650\nSame Issue on v4.6 stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindow 10 x64 Latest - Godot v4.6.1 stable - GTX 1650 - Ryzen 3 3100\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen resizing any dock panel (Scene Tree, Inspector, FileSystem, History, Bottom Panel, etc.), the resize operation stops immediately if the mouse cursor enters the 3D viewport while still dragging.\n\nThis issue affects all dock panels and only occurs when interacting near the 3D viewport. Resizing works correctly when dragging in directions that do not cross into the 3D viewport.\n\nThe issue does NOT occur in:\n2D viewport\nScript editor\nScene editor UI areas\n\nThe issue ONLY occurs when the cursor enters the 3D viewport.\nThis suggests the 3D viewport is capturing or interrupting mouse drag events during active UI resize operations.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open any 3D project\n2. Ensure 3D viewport is visible\n3. Hover mouse over resize grab bar of any dock panel. Examples: [ Scene Tree, Inspector, FileSystem, Bottom Panel ]\n4. Click and hold mouse button to resize\n5. While still holding mouse button, move cursor into the 3D viewport\n6. Observe resizing stops immediately\n\nExpected result\n- Resize operation continues normally regardless of cursor entering viewport\n- Dock resizing remains active until mouse button is released\n\nActual result\n- Resize operation stops immediately when cursor enters 3D viewport\n- User must release mouse and start drag again\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nSimple New Project will do.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/use